{
  "concept": "Expanding the merge-sort recurrence T(n) = 2T(n/2) + cn into a recursion tree shows that every level costs exactly cn, so the total cost is the level cost times the tree height lg n, giving Θ(n lg n).",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "Stage label (a): the single term T(n) printed alone at upper left",
    "Stage label (b): root node cn with two straight edges down to two leaf terms T(n/2) and T(n/2)",
    "Stage label (c): root cn branching to two cn/2 nodes, each branching to two T(n/4) terms (four T(n/4) total)",
    "Stage label (d): the fully expanded tree — root cn, level-1 pair cn/2 and cn/2, level-2 quartet of four cn/4 nodes",
    "Short dashed continuation edges descending from each cn/4 node toward the omitted middle levels",
    "Vertical dotted connector lines standing in for the undrawn levels",
    "Bottom row of leaf nodes each labeled c, with a horizontal ellipsis '...' through the middle of the row",
    "Curly brace beneath the leaf row labeled n (number of leaves)",
    "Double-headed vertical arrow at far left spanning the full tree height, labeled 'lg n'",
    "Dotted horizontal arrows from each drawn level pointing right to that level's cost label",
    "Right-hand column of level sums: cn, cn, cn, vertical ellipsis, cn",
    "Horizontal rule beneath the right-hand column",
    "Total annotation: 'Total: cn lg n + cn'",
    "Small caption letters (a), (b), (c), (d) positioned under their respective panels",
    "Recurrence reminder text T(n) = 2T(n/2) + cn",
    "Highlight band / row shading used when the level-cost overlay is on"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "expansionStage",
      "type": "button",
      "label": "Expand the recurrence",
      "states": ["T(n)", "one split", "two splits", "full tree"],
      "default": "T(n)",
      "teaches": "Each expansion step substitutes the recurrence into itself: an unresolved T(k) term is replaced by a cost node ck plus two children T(k/2), which is exactly how the tree is generated."
    },
    {
      "id": "problemSize",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "Problem size n (powers of 2)",
      "range": [4, 1024, 1],
      "default": 16,
      "teaches": "Doubling n adds exactly one level to the tree and doubles the number of leaves, so height grows as lg n while each level's cost stays cn."
    },
    {
      "id": "levelCostOverlay",
      "type": "toggle",
      "label": "Level-cost overlay",
      "options": ["off", "on"],
      "default": "off",
      "teaches": "Every level has twice as many nodes each costing half as much, so all levels sum to the same cn — and the grand total is therefore just cn times the number of levels."
    },
    {
      "id": "inspectNode",
      "type": "hover",
      "teaches": "Each node's label encodes both its subproblem size and its non-recursive merge cost, so the reader can see that node cost = c × (subproblem size)."
    }
  ],
  "demo_steps": [
    {
      "title": "(a) Start with T(n)",
      "narration": "The whole running time is a single unknown term T(n). Nothing is expanded yet — this is the recurrence in its most compact form.",
      "state": { "expansionStage": "T(n)", "levelCostOverlay": "off", "problemSize": 16 }
    },
    {
      "title": "(b) One substitution",
      "narration": "Applying T(n) = 2T(n/2) + cn once splits the term into a root of merge cost cn with two unresolved children T(n/2). The cn is the work done at this level only.",
      "state": { "expansionStage": "one split", "levelCostOverlay": "off", "problemSize": 16 }
    },
    {
      "title": "(c) Two substitutions",
      "narration": "Expanding both children turns each T(n/2) into a cost node cn/2 with two T(n/4) children. Notice the second level has two nodes of cost cn/2 — already summing to cn.",
      "state": { "expansionStage": "two splits", "levelCostOverlay": "off", "problemSize": 16 }
    },
    {
      "title": "(d) The full tree",
      "narration": "Keep substituting until every leaf is a base case of cost c. There are n leaves along the bottom, and the double-headed arrow on the left marks the height as lg n.",
      "state": { "expansionStage": "full tree", "levelCostOverlay": "off", "problemSize": 16 }
    },
    {
      "title": "Add up each level",
      "narration": "Turn on the overlay: each row lights up and its dotted arrow reports the same total, cn. Node counts double while node costs halve, so the product never changes.",
      "state": { "expansionStage": "full tree", "levelCostOverlay": "on", "problemSize": 16 }
    },
    {
      "title": "Grow n and watch the height",
      "narration": "Slide n upward by powers of two: the leaf row lengthens to n leaves and the tree gains one level per doubling. The total lg n + 1 levels each cost cn, so Total = cn lg n + cn.",
      "state": { "expansionStage": "full tree", "levelCostOverlay": "on", "problemSize": 256 }
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "Doubling the number of nodes while halving each node's cost keeps every level at exactly cn, so the total cost is simply cn times the number of levels — and the number of levels is lg n.",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Top third: three small panels side by side labeled (a), (b), (c) in italic serif math type, on white with thin black edges — (a) is just 'T(n)' at the far upper left, (b) a root 'cn' with two straight edges to 'T(n/2)' twice, (c) a three-level tree with root 'cn', two 'cn/2', and four 'T(n/4)'. Lower two-thirds: panel (d), a wide binary tree centered horizontally — root cn, two cn/2, four cn/4, then short dashed edges fading downward, vertical dotted lines, and a bottom row of 'c' leaves with a centered '...' ellipsis. A curly brace spans the leaf row labeled 'n'. A tall double-headed arrow on the far left spans root to leaves, labeled 'lg n'. To the right of each drawn level, a horizontal dotted arrow with a small arrowhead points to a right-aligned column of level sums, all reading 'cn', with a vertical ellipsis between the cn/4 row and the leaf row. A short horizontal rule under that column is followed by 'Total: cn lg n + cn'. All math in italic serif; base figure is pure black on white. Interactive additions: resolved cost nodes in dark blue, still-unresolved T(...) terms in muted gray-orange to signal 'not yet expanded'; the level-cost overlay draws a soft amber horizontal band across the active row and bolds its cn label; the lg n arrow label updates with the concrete numeric height as the n slider moves, and the total line updates to show both the symbolic and numeric value."
}

