      }
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "Doubling the number of nodes while halving each node's cost keeps every level at exactly cn, so the total is cn times the number of levels — and doubling n adds exactly one level, which is why the number of levels is lg n.",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Single wide panel showing one evolving tree, with the current stage caption (a)/(b)/(c)/(d) in small italic serif at the bottom-left of the drawing; prior stages may be echoed as tiny thumbnails but the main area is one large tree so labels stay legible. Keep the viewBox tight — minimal padding — so node labels render at 12 px or larger at inline width; the cost labels (cn, cn/2, cn/4, c) and the right-hand level sums are the largest text, clearly bigger than the (a)-(d) caption letters and the recurrence reminder. Tree: root 'cn' at top center, two 'cn/2' below, four 'cn/4' below that; from each cn/4 node a short heavy dashed edge descends toward omitted levels, with bold vertical dotted stand-in lines and a vertical ellipsis in the gap. Bottom row has a full set of 'c' leaves — for n = 8 draw all eight, with the horizontal '...' placed in the gap between the fourth and fifth leaves rather than substituting for a leaf. A curly brace under the leaf row is labeled 'n'. A tall double-headed arrow at the far left spans root to leaves labeled 'lg n' (plus the concrete numeric height). To the right of every drawn level, a dotted horizontal arrow points to a right-aligned column of level sums all reading 'cn', with a vertical ellipsis before the leaf row's cn; a short horizontal rule closes the column above 'Total: cn lg n + cn'. All math in italic serif, base figure black on white. Interactive coloring: resolved cost nodes dark blue, still-unresolved T(...) terms muted gray-orange; during a substitution the replaced T(k) fades out as its ck node and two children fade in; the level-cost overlay paints a soft amber band across the active row and bolds its cn label. Every element tied to n — leaf count, brace label, number of drawn levels, height arrow span, number of cost arrows and cn entries, total line — regenerates when the height slider moves."
